depgraph: merge order of PDEPEND children no longer depends on the hash seed

Sub-series: P (stage 5) - patch 3 of 3; applies without 0035 and 0036, in any order with them.
Base: upstream bdf046b03 with 0001-0034 (the defect is in unpatched upstream too).

In _serialize_tasks(), "for child in medium_post:" iterates a set of Package
objects whose hashes derive from str hashes, so the order in which PDEPEND
children are appended to asap_nodes, and with it their place in the merge
list, changed with PYTHONHASHSEED from run to run. Seen on the test image:
llvm-core/llvmgold-23 and llvm-core/llvm-toolchain-symlinks-23 (both PDEPEND
children of llvm-core/llvm) swapped places between runs of the same emerge,
with unpatched upstream and with the series alike. The loop now follows the
graph's child order. The result is one of the orders the set iteration could
produce; nothing else reads this order.

No effect on the resolve time (88.8 -> 89.1 s, 90.6 -> 91.8 s: noise).
Reported by the agent: full merge order equal for every seed tried (0, 1, 2,
3, 6, 7 and random) where unpatched upstream gave two orders.

Origin: written by AI agents (Claude) in the emerge-fast job, stage 5, 2026-11-24
(two rounds of implementer agents, black-box tester agents and a timing judge);
split into independent patches and re-checked on 2026-11-24. Not a human-written
change. Base: upstream bdf046b03 with patches 0001-0034. Test: `emerge -p -uND
@world` on six states of one system image, six resolves in parallel; every run
gave the same merge list in order and the same number of backtracking attempts
as unpatched bdf046b03.

--- a/lib/_emerge/depgraph.py
+++ b/lib/_emerge/depgraph.py
@@ -11565,6 +11565,20 @@
                         )
                     )
                     medium_post -= medium_post_satisifed
+                    if len(medium_post) > 1:
+                        # stage5: medium_post is a set of Package objects, whose
+                        # hashes derive from str hashes, so its iteration order
+                        # (and with it the order in which PDEPEND children are
+                        # appended to asap_nodes, i.e. their merge order) changed
+                        # with PYTHONHASHSEED from run to run. Iterate in the
+                        # graph's (deterministic) child order instead. The
+                        # result is one of the orders that the set iteration
+                        # could produce; nothing else reads this order.
+                        medium_post = [
+                            child
+                            for child in mygraph.child_nodes(node)
+                            if child in medium_post
+                        ]
                     for child in medium_post:
                         if child in selected_nodes:
                             continue
